; BTN-1 (2026-09-19) — THE CONFIRM BUTTON ("I'M DONE HIDING"), on the −X wall.
;
; MOUNTING: local +Z out of the wall, into the room — see HoldingRoom.tscn's StartButton header
; for why every button in this level is authored that way. This wall faces +X, so the basis is a
; quarter turn about Y and its twelve floats are (0,0,1, 0,1,0, −1,0,0). Those are basis ROWS
; (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md): the same rotation written column-wise is its inverse and would
; point the button, its label and its cap travel INTO the wall. The server prints the measured
; facing at world build ("[buttons] found Confirm button at … facing …") so this is checkable
; from a log rather than only from a render.
;
; x = −6.94 is the wall's inner face (−7.0) plus the plate's own half-depth. z = −3 puts it well
; clear of the four SearchSpawn markers and of every coordinate Run-PlaceTest.ps1 drives a bot to.
;
; ONLY THE HIDER CAN PRESS IT, and in a real session only the hider is ever in this room while it
; is live — the gate is still enforced (RoundButtonRules.Gate), because "unreachable in practice"
; and "refused" are different guarantees and only the second survives a level edit.

[node name="ConfirmButton" type="StaticBody3D" parent="." groups=["pressable", "round_button", "round_button_confirm"]]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, -6.94, 1.15, -3)
script = ExtResource("4_button")

